{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773342108,"nonce":"BACrbvTtpsmdU4Cy8eAlyhmLTkQ=","title":"auth-merge.sh: hardcoded ../../../../bin/dwt path breaks in worktrees","message":"auth-merge.sh references dwt and pre-auth-check via relative paths like `../../../../bin/dwt` anchored to cli/ directory depth. This assumption breaks if the repo is run from a worktree at a different depth, or if the bin/ location changes.\n\nIdentified during dispatcher-in-repo refactor. Fix: use MANDIBLE_BIN_DIR derived from the dispatcher (exported as env var) or resolve via git rev-parse --show-toplevel from within the script.\n\nGemini noted: \"The current auth-merge.sh uses a hardcoded relative path which assumes it is being run from a specific depth. If run from a worktree, this path is likely broken.\"","files":null}]}